<h1><%= h(@community.name) %>: script endpoints</h1>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Script endpoints</h2>
  <p class="muted">
    An endpoint is a web address you give a name to. A script can then call that name with
    <code>rubotty.async_http</code> and never knows the address, the API key, or anything else you put
    here. That is the point: you decide what this community can reach out to, and somebody writing a
    rule cannot widen it.
  </p>
  <p class="muted">
    Headers are where a key belongs. They are sent with every request and are never shown to a script,
    never in a reply, and never in a script trace.
  </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <a href="<%= url("/communities/#{@community.slug}/endpoints/new") %>"><button type="button">Add endpoint</button></a>
</div>

<% if @endpoints.empty? %>
  <div class="card muted">
    No script endpoints yet, so <code>rubotty.async_http</code> has nothing to call. Add one and a script can
    reach it by name.
  </div>
<% else %>
  <div class="card">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Method</th><th>Address</th><th>State</th><th></th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @endpoints.each do |endpoint| %>
          <tr>
            <td>
              <a href="<%= url("/communities/#{@community.slug}/endpoints/#{endpoint.id}") %>"><%= h(endpoint.name) %></a>
              <% if endpoint.description.to_s != "" %>
                <div class="muted"><%= h(endpoint.description) %></div>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td><code><%= h(endpoint.http_method) %></code></td>
            <td class="muted"><%= h(endpoint.url) %></td>
            <td><span class="pill <%= endpoint.enabled ? "on" : "off" %>"><%= endpoint.enabled ? "on" : "off" %></span></td>
            <td>
              <form class="inline" method="post"
                    action="<%= url("/communities/#{@community.slug}/endpoints/#{endpoint.id}/delete") %>">
                <%= act_button("Delete", :manage_endpoints, community: @community, style: "danger") %>
              </form>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
<% end %>
